{
  "name": "scatter_greek",
  "description": "Greek — Modern Standard Greek, written in the Greek alphabet. Phonemic inventory on the standardized 12-column place axis. The distinctive feature on this atlas is the interdental fricative pair (θ, ð) — preserved from Ancient Greek in the same column where most other comparison languages are empty. Voiceless and voiced stop pairs at 3 places (bilabial, dental, velar). Two nasals. Voiceless fricatives f, θ, s, x; voiced v, ð, z, ɣ. Affricates ts, dz (alveolar; no post-alveolar /tʃ dʒ/ — Modern Greek lacks the post-alveolar series most other IE comparison languages have). Lateral /l/, trill /r/, palatal /j/. Inventory drawn from Holton, Mackridge & Philippaki-Warburton (2012).",
